This is a short clip from a two-person interview: one person on the LEFT half of the screen, one on the RIGHT half. The audio contains exactly one speaker's voice for this turn.

## Task

Decide who is speaking in this clip: listen to the voice and watch both people's mouths — the speaker's lips move in sync with the voice; the listener's mouth stays still.

Answer `"left"`, `"right"`, or `"unclear"` (only when genuinely impossible to tell).

## Output format

Output only valid JSON:

{
  "speaker": "left" | "right" | "unclear"
}

Output JSON only — no markdown, no commentary.
